{"timestamp":1774892396667,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"36383ca3-7049-442c-a553-e390a4b95a57","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BY6hTQWYTsPi58cvxR7JiX","payload":{"session_id":"36383ca3-7049-442c-a553-e390a4b95a57","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-c39aac7b/36383ca3-7049-442c-a553-e390a4b95a57.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/c39aac7b","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/c39aac7b/.pinata/specs/issue-11-adw-c39aac7b-sdlc_planner-prevent-duplicate-fragment-title-clone.md","content":"# Plan: Prevent Duplicate Fragment Title for Cloned Cards in M@S Studio\n\n## Summary\nWhen a card is cloned in M@S Studio, the cloned fragment inherits the original title, which can create duplicates within the same tag path. This plan adds a uniqueness check that automatically appends a numeric suffix (`-1`, `-2`, \u2026) to the cloned fragment's title before saving, scoped to the parent folder path. Manual title edits entered by the author in the clone dialog are not altered.\n\n## Task Description\n- Initialize the clone dialog title field with the source fragment's title (currently blank, so no-op saves go through unchanged).\n- Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle, path)` to `mas-repository.js` that strips any existing `-N` suffix, searches existing fragment titles at the given path, and returns the lowest available `baseTitle-N` candidate.\n- Call this helper inside `copyFragment` in `mas-repository.js` to resolve the final title before saving.\n- Apply the same `titleClone` initialization fix to `editor-panel.js`, which contains a parallel clone flow.\n- Add unit tests for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`.\n\n## Relevant Files\n\n| File | Action | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| `studio/src/mas-repository.js` | Edit | Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`; use it in `copyFragment` |\n| `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` | Edit | Initialize `titleClone` to `this.fragment.title` in `showClone()` |\n| `studio/src/editor-panel.js` | Edit | Same fix for parallel clone dialog in EditorPanel component |\n| `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` | Edit | Unit tests for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` |\n\n## Step by Step Tasks\n\n### 1. Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` to `mas-repository.js`\n\nAdd a new async method to `MasRepository` (above `copyFragment`):\n\n```js\nasync generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle, path) {\n    // Strip existing numeric suffix: \"card-2\" -> \"card\"\n    const suffixMatch = baseTitle.match(/^(.*)-(\\d+)$/);\n    const rootTitle = suffixMatch ? suffixMatch[1] : baseTitle;\n\n    // Collect all fragment titles at the given path\n    const existingTitles = new Set();\n    try {\n        const gen = this.aem.sites.cf.fragments.search({ path, query: rootTitle });\n        for await (const items of gen) {\n            for (const item of items) {\n                existingTitles.add(item.title);\n            }\n        }\n    } catch {\n        return baseTitle; // Search failure: return original, do not block clone\n    }\n\n    if (!existingTitles.has(baseTitle)) return baseTitle;\n\n    let n = 1;\n    while (n <= 99) {\n        const candidate = `${rootTitle}-${n}`;\n        if (!existingTitles.has(candidate)) return candidate;\n        n++;\n    }\n    return `${rootTitle}-${n}`;\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Use the helper in `copyFragment` in `mas-repository.js`\n\nInside `copyFragment`, after the `copy(this.fragmentInEdit)` call resolves, derive the parent path from `result.path` and generate a unique title:\n\n- Compute `const parentPath = result.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/');`\n- Compute `const requestedTitle = (updatedTitle && updatedTitle !== result.title) ? updatedTitle : result.title;`\n- Await `const uniqueTitle = await this.generateUniqueFragmentTitle(requestedTitle, parentPath);`\n- Replace the `needsSave` block so that if `uniqueTitle !== result.title || osi`, the title is set to `uniqueTitle` and a save is performed.\n\nThis ensures that even when the author leaves the title unchanged in the dialog, the cloned fragment gets a unique title.\n\n### 3. Initialize `titleClone` in `showClone()` \u2014 `mas-fragment-editor.js`\n\nIn `MasFragmentEditor.showClone()`:\n```js\nasync showClone() {\n    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {\n        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();\n        if (!confirmed) return;\n    }\n    this.titleClone = this.fragment.title;  // <-- add this line\n    this.showCloneDialog = true;\n    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);\n}\n```\n\nThis ensures `titleClone` carries the current title when the dialog opens, so the correct value is passed to `copyFragment` when the author clicks \"Clone\" without typing.\n\n### 4. Initialize `titleClone` in `showClone()` \u2014 `editor-panel.js`\n\nApply the identical one-line fix to `EditorPanel.showClone()` (line ~620) for the parallel clone flow used in the side-by-side editor panel:\n\n```js\nasync showClone() {\n    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {\n        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();\n        if (!confirmed) return;\n    }\n    this.titleClone = this.fragment.title;  // <-- add this line\n    this.showCloneDialog = true;\n    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Add unit tests in `mas-repository.test.js`\n\nAdd a new `describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle')` block inside the existing test suite. Cover:\n\n- Returns `baseTitle` unchanged when no fragments match at the path.\n- Returns `baseTitle-1` when `baseTitle` already exists but `baseTitle-1` does not.\n- Returns `baseTitle-2` when both `baseTitle` and `baseTitle-1` already exist.\n- Strips an existing numeric suffix before incrementing: `baseTitle-1` \u2192 `baseTitle-2` (not `baseTitle-1-1`).\n- Returns `baseTitle` (no throw) when the AEM search call rejects.\n\nTest pattern (using existing sinon + esm-bundle/chai setup):\n```js\ndescribe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle', () => {\n    it('returns the base title when no duplicate exists', async () => { \u2026 });\n    it('appends -1 when base title already exists', async () => { \u2026 });\n    it('increments to -2 when -1 already exists', async () => { \u2026 });\n    it('strips existing suffix before incrementing', async () => { \u2026 });\n    it('returns base title when search fails', async () => { \u2026 });\n});\n```\n\nUse `sandbox.stub()` on `repository.aem.sites.cf.fragments.search` to return an async generator that yields mock title arrays.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Cloning a card with an existing Fragment Title generates a unique title with a `-N` suffix.\n- The suffix increments correctly: `-1`, `-2`, `-3` for successive clones.\n- Uniqueness is scoped to the parent folder path (same as the source fragment).\n- The original card's Fragment Title is not modified.\n- Authors can still type a custom title in the clone dialog; that value is deduplicated if needed but otherwise honored.\n- No two cards share the same Fragment Title + folder path after a clone operation.\n\n## Validation Commands\n- `node --check studio/src/mas-repository.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`\n- `node --check studio/src/editor-panel.js`\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BY6hTQWYTsPi58cvxR7JiX"}}
